# Aston Martin Virage coupe, 1989-1994.
#
# The John Heffernan and Ken Greenley Virage: the slab-sided Towns-era body
# replaced by a wide, square-shouldered coupe with rectangular Audi 100-type
# headlamps, a slat grille with the winged badge, a flat bonnet with a central
# crease, and rectangular tail lamp clusters with a body-coloured centre panel.
# 411 coupes built; the Virage Volante is a different body and is not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_Virage
#
# Dimensions 4.735 x 1.855 x 1.320 m, wheelbase 2.610 m.
#
# Shape reference: a green 1994 coupe in a 30-degree front three-quarter (there
# is NO true side elevation in the pack), a 1991 Cumberland Grey car in front
# three-quarter, and a blue Swiss car in rear three-quarter. The flank and the
# wheelbase are therefore estimated from the three views and the published
# dimensions; the limitation is recorded rather than hidden.
#
# Colours: grade (c). Cumberland Grey (the 1991 car), Snowden White, Hunter
# Green and Suffolk Red are named on documented period cars; black is recorded
# on the 6.3 Widebody. Weights 3, 3, 2, 2, total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 255 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70: a wide 2+2 with a
# more upright cabin than the V8 Vantage. Class 4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1989 intro, retires staggered 2007-2010 on an
# eighteen- to twenty-one-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-virage.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-virage.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-virage/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side elevation in the pack, so the
# flank and wheelbase are estimated from the three views and the published
# dimensions. The front lamp housings and lower intake project slightly instead
# of reading as inset. At 128 px the slab sides, rectangular lamps and tail
# panel read as a Virage.

